##RenderMan RIB-Structure 1.0
# A 480-segment toroidal spiral, the scene SC-012 exists for: a large
# bounding box whose surface occupies a small fraction of it. A dense grid
# over the bound could not afford this, which is why extraction is a seeded
# continuation walk that visits only the cells the surface actually crosses.
# The blobby statistics measure that directly: rendered here, the walk
# visits 2.77% of the cells a dense grid over the same extent would have
# had, while emitting 278,024 triangles from 480 fields. That percentage is
# the instrument -- a walk that had degenerated into sweeping the volume
# climbs towards 100, which no wall-clock reading would attribute correctly.
#
# Spec 015-blobby-implicit-surfaces, T096. One variant per camera hider; the
# same three files serve both the visual and the parity registrations.
version 3.03
Hider "raytrace"
Display "blobby-spiral-raytrace.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 240 240 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" 30
Clipping 0.1 1000
Translate 0 0 20
WorldBegin
    LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.2]
    LightSource "distantlight" 2 "intensity" [0.9] "from" [5 5 -5] "to" [0 0 0]
    Color [0.72 0.74 0.85]
    Surface "matte"
    ShadingInterpolation "smooth"
    Attribute "blobby" "float tolerance" [ 0.09 ]
    Rotate 22 1 0 0
    Blobby 480 [
